  "description": "Biomedical Instrumentation teaches students how physiological variables become reliable clinical data. Students study electrodes, sensors, analog front ends, filters, data conversion, embedded acquisition, noise control, safety, calibration, validation, interoperability, cybersecurity, and applied measurements such as ECG, EMG, EEG, pressure, flow, optical sensing, and chemical biosensing.",
